Tropospheric delay in myb (ext/troposphere)

The models are those of the IERS Conventions (2010), chapter 9 (G. Petit, B. Luzum (eds.), IERS
Technical Note No. 36, Verlag des Bundesamts fuer Kartographie und Geodaesie, 2010, with the
updates at https://iers-conventions.obspm.fr/):

  - J. Saastamoinen, "Atmospheric correction for the troposphere and stratosphere in radio
    ranging of satellites", Geophys. Monogr. 15, AGU, 1972, in the form of J. L. Davis et al.,
    Radio Sci. 20, 1593, 1985;
  - V. B. Mendes, E. C. Pavlis, "High-accuracy zenith delay prediction at optical wavelengths",
    Geophys. Res. Lett. 31, L14602, 2004;
  - V. B. Mendes, G. Prates, E. C. Pavlis, D. E. Pavlis, R. B. Langley, "Improved mapping
    functions for atmospheric refraction correction in SLR", Geophys. Res. Lett. 29, 1414, 2002
    (FCULa; coefficients of table 9.1 of the Conventions);
  - J. Boehm, B. Werl, H. Schuh, "Troposphere mapping functions for GPS and very long baseline
    interferometry from European Centre for Medium-Range Weather Forecasts operational analysis
    data", J. Geophys. Res. 111, B02406, 2006 (VMF1);
  - J. Boehm, A. Niell, P. Tregoning, H. Schuh, "Global Mapping Function (GMF): A new empirical
    mapping function based on numerical weather model data", Geophys. Res. Lett. 33, L07304,
    2006;
  - J. Boehm, R. Heinkelmann, H. Schuh, "Short Note: A global model of pressure and temperature
    for geodetic applications", J. Geod. 81, 679, 2007 (GPT);
  - A. E. Niell, "Global mapping functions for the atmosphere delay at radio wavelengths",
    J. Geophys. Res. 101, 3227, 1996 (height correction, seasonal phase);
  - G. Chen, T. A. Herring, "Effects of atmospheric azimuthal asymmetry on the analysis of space
    geodetic data", J. Geophys. Res. 102, 20489, 1997 (gradient mapping function).

troposphere.c is written by the authors of myb from these published equations; it is not a
translation of the IERS Conventions software (whose licence is not BSD-compatible). The
coefficient tables of GMF and GPT in troposphere_tables.inc are numbers (model data, like the
tables of the Conventions used elsewhere in myb) taken from the DATA statements of GMF.F and
GPT.F of the Conventions software, chapter 9, identified by SHA-256 in that file. The test cases
in the headers of FCUL_ZD_HPA.F, FCUL_A.F, VMF1.F, VMF1_HT.F, GMF.F and GPT.F serve as the
reference of tests/ext/test_troposphere.c.
